1687
00:51:47,722 --> 00:51:49,733
- The people there scream so much.
- Oh, but…

1688
00:51:49,734 --> 00:51:51,700
Was it set up like this
yesterday too?

1689
00:51:51,701 --> 00:51:53,808
[At least the staff pitched the tents for them today]
No, we set them up.

1690
00:51:53,809 --> 00:51:54,696
We set them up yesterday.

1691
00:51:55,167 --> 00:51:58,033
[And the one person who's seeing
the paupers' accommodation for the very first time]

1692
00:51:58,600 --> 00:52:00,367
[DAWN] How are 3 people
supposed to sleep in here?

1693
00:52:00,900 --> 00:52:03,233
[The blue-blooded prince
who's only slept on comfy beds]

1694
00:52:04,267 --> 00:52:06,300
[The pauper tent
feels so unfamiliar]

1695
00:52:06,500 --> 00:52:07,900
Alright, head inside!

1696
00:52:07,901 --> 00:52:09,500
- Goodnight!
- Okay, Pauper #1.

1697
00:52:09,900 --> 00:52:14,433
[The experienced paupers naturally walk in]
I was Prince #2 yesterday, though.

1698
00:52:14,600 --> 00:52:15,900
It's nice that
our accommodations are close by!

1699
00:52:15,901 --> 00:52:17,186
Is... is that so...?

1700
00:52:17,187 --> 00:52:18,106
Is that so?

1701
00:52:18,107 --> 00:52:19,192
I guess, yeah.

1702
00:52:20,167 --> 00:52:22,916
[The Paupert naturally heads into the tent too]
Oh, my legs hurt. Oh, my legs.

1703
00:52:22,917 --> 00:52:25,200
After being the pauper a few times,

1704
00:52:25,201 --> 00:52:28,132
[Now it feels like home]
It felt very familiar, stepping into the tent.

1705
00:52:28,133 --> 00:52:29,582
Hey, but it must be
nice and cool here.

1706
00:52:29,583 --> 00:52:31,091
[With mocking words of comfort]
Yeah, it's nice and windy today.

1707
00:52:31,092 --> 00:52:33,390
[and worry]
Hey, be careful! Don't get pushed toward the back.

1708
00:52:33,391 --> 00:52:34,713
Hey, but shall we finish up

1709
00:52:34,714 --> 00:52:36,433
[They leave their little pauper brothers]
our conversation from earlier here?

1710
00:52:36,434 --> 00:52:37,567
- LEETEUK, let's go.
- Let's go.

1711
00:52:37,568 --> 00:52:38,500
[The princes head to the cruise]
Good night!

1712
00:52:38,501 --> 00:52:40,167
- Bye!
- Sleep well!

1713
00:52:40,168 --> 00:52:41,067
Good night.

1714
00:52:41,397 --> 00:52:43,312
[Though the princes have left...]
What’s with the music!

1715
00:52:43,313 --> 00:52:45,614
- It's really loud! How are we supposed to sleep?
- They're just pumping up the music!

1716
00:52:46,209 --> 00:52:47,896
[No such thing as a dull moment in the pauper's tent]
A woodpecker on the left, and a club on the right.

1717
00:52:47,897 --> 00:52:48,924
I'm gonna go crazy.

1718
00:52:49,867 --> 00:52:52,400
We just went
straight into the tent.

1719
00:52:52,401 --> 00:52:55,500
But... the music
was just way too loud.

1720
00:52:55,790 --> 00:52:58,494
[The music and the lights were absolutely unbearable]
It was like a full-on festival.

1721
00:52:58,495 --> 00:53:00,400
The lights were super flashy.

1722
00:53:00,807 --> 00:53:02,182
[Couldn't resist and attended the party]
We got curious, so we went to check it out.

1723
00:53:02,183 --> 00:53:03,875
It felt kind of like a banquet.

1724
00:53:04,495 --> 00:53:09,332
The locals suddenly
appeared and started dancing.

1725
00:53:09,867 --> 00:53:11,410
[YOHAN feels out of his element here]

1726
00:53:11,411 --> 00:53:12,833
I can't do this!

1727
00:53:12,834 --> 00:53:15,700
[Standing still when everyone's dancing?]
It's awkward to stand around while everyone's dancing.

1728
00:53:15,701 --> 00:53:17,995
[I’m the main dancer of NCT DREAM, you know?]
So, I just threw in some waves,

1729
00:53:17,996 --> 00:53:19,308
and did stuff like this.

1730
00:53:19,309 --> 00:53:21,295
I did some finger-tutting.

1731
00:53:21,296 --> 00:53:22,683
I did stuff like that.

1732
00:53:23,367 --> 00:53:27,267
[A pro dancer steps up
at the Egyptian neighborhood dance party]

1733
00:53:28,367 --> 00:53:32,167
[And the one stealing
the spotlight behind him]

1734
00:53:34,033 --> 00:53:36,767
[Lost in the moment]

1735
00:53:36,768 --> 00:53:39,567
I did slightly bust a move or two.

1736
00:53:39,568 --> 00:53:42,667
[Born to be an idol]
I realized I'm quite the attention-seeker too.

1737
00:53:43,394 --> 00:53:45,100
[This kind of moment is the fun of traveling]
In the middle of all that, I'm sleepy.

1738
00:53:45,108 --> 00:53:46,408
- I'm really sleepy.
- Right, I'm a bit sleepy.

1739
00:53:46,409 --> 00:53:47,400
I just wanna sleep.

1740
00:53:47,800 --> 00:53:49,300
I just wanna sleep
even without a sleeping bag.

1741
00:53:49,912 --> 00:53:51,096
[Using a sleeping bag as a pillow tonight]
Should we go for that vibe today?

1742
00:53:51,102 --> 00:53:52,598
I think you're right.
It'll be comfier to use as a pillow.

1743
00:53:52,601 --> 00:53:53,767
But from what I can see,

1744
00:53:53,768 --> 00:53:56,367
- we'll use the sleeping bag when it gets cold at dawn.
- Oh, really?

1745
00:53:56,368 --> 00:53:58,312
[Still, let's just lie down for now]
But for now, let's just do it like this.

1746
00:53:58,313 --> 00:53:59,598
- Oh, like that.
- Okay, okay.

1747
00:54:00,567 --> 00:54:02,197
[The experienced paupers
lock up for the night]

1748
00:54:02,198 --> 00:54:02,924
Wow.

1749
00:54:05,192 --> 00:54:06,800
[No, but…]
This is actually comfy.

1750
00:54:06,801 --> 00:54:08,933
We're gonna sleep
with this music blasting?!

1751
00:54:08,934 --> 00:54:11,067
Like, isn't it too noisy?

1752
00:54:11,068 --> 00:54:12,467
I think I can sleep.

1753
00:54:12,857 --> 00:54:14,633
No, but this is so loud…

1754
00:54:14,634 --> 00:54:16,600
I think I can sleep.

1755
00:54:16,601 --> 00:54:21,732
Honestly, this isn't so bad,
because on the first day…

1756
00:54:21,733 --> 00:54:23,015
[These two who were paupers on Day 1…]
Oh, wait…

1757
00:54:23,016 --> 00:54:24,367
This is legit pauper status.

1758
00:54:24,633 --> 00:54:26,300
[experienced the desert tent]
Are we seriously stranded here?

1759
00:54:26,793 --> 00:54:27,613
That was legendary.

1760
00:54:27,614 --> 00:54:29,088
[Just counting their blessings today]
This isn't bad at all.

1761
00:54:29,089 --> 00:54:30,433
- That’s why I’m feeling good right now
- Oh, really?

1762
00:54:31,067 --> 00:54:34,067
[The Day 2 pauper doesn't get it]
Oh, today… Well, yesterday was pretty okay.

1763
00:54:34,068 --> 00:54:36,315
- Day 2 paupers were just kings.
- If you were there yesterday,

1764
00:54:36,316 --> 00:54:38,500
- you would've loved it.
- Yesterday, it was king status.

1765
00:54:38,673 --> 00:54:39,580
No.

1766
00:54:39,986 --> 00:54:41,700
You’ve never been a prince before.

1767
00:54:41,701 --> 00:54:43,333
(Paupert)
Maybe that’s why…

1768
00:54:45,418 --> 00:54:47,600
I can see them back there!

1769
00:54:47,601 --> 00:54:48,998
I can see them totally loving it.

1770
00:54:49,988 --> 00:54:52,500
[Watching the princes across the river]
The first day was seriously legendary.

1771
00:54:52,514 --> 00:54:54,217
Oh, they're picking rooms!

1772
00:54:55,693 --> 00:54:56,812
[The princes inside the cruise]
Oh man.

1773
00:54:56,813 --> 00:54:58,300
- It just feels like my house now.
- Oh!

1774
00:54:58,301 --> 00:54:59,993
[So moved by the soft couch]
OH! Why is this sofa so comfy?

1775
00:54:59,994 --> 00:55:01,993
Wow, this is amazing.

1776
00:55:02,194 --> 00:55:04,067
- Let's pick our rooms.
- How did you pick yesterday?

1777
00:55:04,068 --> 00:55:05,110
[The princes will pick rooms again today]
We just put the keys here

1778
00:55:05,111 --> 00:55:06,600
- and played Rock-Paper-Scissors to decide.
- Oh, okay.

1779
00:55:06,601 --> 00:55:09,799
[Only SHINDONG switched in]
Oh, I'm the only new guest here.

1780
00:55:09,912 --> 00:55:11,170
[Feeling at home now]
If you want something to drink,

1781
00:55:11,171 --> 00:55:13,045
you can have a drink at night.

1782
00:55:13,111 --> 00:55:14,084
Excuse me!

1783
00:55:15,204 --> 00:55:16,791
[Naturally ordering a refreshing cola]
One Coke, please.

1784
00:55:16,792 --> 00:55:18,500
Two Cokes, please.

1785
00:55:18,501 --> 00:55:19,200
SHINDONG, are you good?

1786
00:55:19,201 --> 00:55:22,366
[Quickly adjusted]
One Coke Zero.

1787
00:55:22,367 --> 00:55:23,621
Okay, LEETEUK, you pick first.

1788
00:55:23,622 --> 00:55:25,915
[It's really time to pick rooms now]
I really want to sleep in the suite once.

1789
00:55:25,916 --> 00:55:27,792
- Oh!
- Oh, please!

1790
00:55:28,267 --> 00:55:31,400
[Goal: The one and only suite]

1791
00:55:31,600 --> 00:55:33,189
[Relaxed DAWN]
Oh, I have no attachment to it, LEETEUK.

1792
00:55:33,190 --> 00:55:34,296
[and Desperate LEETEUK]
The middle one!

1793
00:55:34,297 --> 00:55:35,600
- Okay.
- Alright.

1794
00:55:35,788 --> 00:55:37,808
[And the former pauper, who's happy with anything but the tent]
Since I'm right-handed, the right one.

1795
00:55:37,809 --> 00:55:39,767
We'll open them
at the count of three.

1796
00:55:39,768 --> 00:55:42,500
[Which prince will get the suite today?]
1, 2, 3!

1797
00:55:42,501 --> 00:55:43,300
Huh?

1798
00:55:43,301 --> 00:55:44,533
[The most earnest]
The suite!

1799
00:55:44,534 --> 00:55:47,333
[LEETEUK gets it!]
Yeah!!

1800
00:55:47,903 --> 00:55:49,100
[Before going to bed]
Okay, let's go.

1801
00:55:49,101 --> 00:55:51,100
- The colas are here. They're here.
- Oh, the cola.

1802
00:55:52,067 --> 00:55:54,700
[Refreshing cola time]
Wow!

1803
00:55:55,030 --> 00:55:56,867
We have to raise a toast.

1804
00:55:58,423 --> 00:56:00,100
[Cheers to the Day 3 princes!]
Congratulations, princes!

1805
00:56:00,101 --> 00:56:02,800
The prince life is so good.

1806
00:56:04,133 --> 00:56:07,733
[After chugging down
a refreshing glass of cola,]

1807
00:56:07,741 --> 00:56:08,593
So refreshing!

1808
00:56:09,197 --> 00:56:10,412
[the princes head off to rest]
Now, rest up!

1809
00:56:10,413 --> 00:56:11,999
Rest well, guys.

1810
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:12,867
Alright, let's go.

1811
00:56:13,815 --> 00:56:16,173
[And out in front…]
This is so nice.

1812
00:56:16,593 --> 00:56:18,133
[The princes are drinking cola…]
I wanna drink some cola.

1813
00:56:18,134 --> 00:56:19,200
Drinks…

1814
00:56:19,201 --> 00:56:21,467
[Let’s just sleep!]
Oh, never mind. Ugh!

1815
00:56:21,822 --> 00:56:23,914
[Sleeping, even with a mouth as dry as a desert]
My mouth has no saliva left, but I'm just gonna sleep.

1816
00:56:23,915 --> 00:56:26,607
Me too.
It's kind of dry right now.

1817
00:56:26,721 --> 00:56:27,500
Should we turn this off?

1818
00:56:27,501 --> 00:56:30,467
[Lights out before bed]
Oh, yes.

1819
00:56:30,689 --> 00:56:31,691
If you click the switch…

1820
00:56:32,391 --> 00:56:34,488
- I know about it too.
- Nice, nice.

1821
00:56:34,489 --> 00:56:37,033
[Gotta get that club lighting at least once]
But doesn't this fit here?

1822
00:56:38,302 --> 00:56:39,095
Ha…

1823
00:56:41,413 --> 00:56:42,700
- I’m like…
- Oh, but like…

1824
00:56:42,701 --> 00:56:45,584
[Their eyes are closing even with the loud music]
But that's starting to sound like a lullaby now.

1825
00:56:45,585 --> 00:56:48,503
I know, right?
It feels like it's telling us to sleep now.

1826
00:56:48,504 --> 00:56:51,767
It was seriously so noisy,
but I was so tired

1827
00:56:51,768 --> 00:56:54,133
that even the noise
sounded like a lullaby.

1828
00:56:54,500 --> 00:56:55,817
[A pauper's night, as explained by the Paupert]
Even as paupers,

1829
00:56:55,818 --> 00:56:58,100
there's no time
to just sit around and complain.

1830
00:56:58,101 --> 00:57:00,295
[Just lie down and sleep]
Let's deal with it tomorrow, and right away…Yeah.

1831
00:57:00,296 --> 00:57:02,500
I passed out
the moment I lay down, so...

1832
00:57:02,501 --> 00:57:04,100
[A tough night for the paupers]
When you have a tough day,

1833
00:57:04,101 --> 00:57:06,733
[always means a deep sleep]
no matter the bed, the sleep is golden.

1834
00:57:06,734 --> 00:57:08,294
We’ve all done this
at least once now.

1835
00:57:08,295 --> 00:57:11,100
[The night falls on
the seasoned paupers...]

1836
00:57:12,033 --> 00:57:14,733
[The princes
head off to bed as well]

1837
00:57:15,806 --> 00:57:19,533
[LEETEUK] I'm using this room?

1838
00:57:20,286 --> 00:57:24,093
[Entering the suite with awe]
Wow!

1839
00:57:24,101 --> 00:57:25,897
Whoa, what is this! Whoa!

1840
00:57:26,898 --> 00:57:28,004
Wow, this is so nice.

1841
00:57:28,005 --> 00:57:29,999
[The best room during the 3 days in Egypt]
What do I do?

1842
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:31,414
I can't believe I'm in a suite!

1843
00:57:31,884 --> 00:57:34,009
Oh, thank you.

1844
00:57:34,505 --> 00:57:35,633
[Nothing to do but be grateful]
Thank you.

1845
00:57:35,634 --> 00:57:36,800
Thank you.

1846
00:57:37,007 --> 00:57:37,813
Thank you.

1847
00:57:38,619 --> 00:57:39,700
Thank you.

1848
00:57:39,867 --> 00:57:42,333
Having peace of mind
is really important in life.

1849
00:57:42,665 --> 00:57:44,200
[Back during his pauper days,]
When I was a pauper on Day 1,

1850
00:57:44,201 --> 00:57:46,533
[he was a hothead]
I kept asking why it had to be like this.

1851
00:57:46,534 --> 00:57:48,567
[His interview on being a pauper on Day 1]
I honestly thought it was too much.

1852
00:57:48,568 --> 00:57:50,367
Like, this seriously isn't right.

1853
00:57:50,500 --> 00:57:51,767
It's just not right.

1854
00:57:51,915 --> 00:57:53,733
[But after becoming a prince]
But the moment I became a prince…!

1855
00:57:53,734 --> 00:57:56,167
[Empathy levels drastically rise]
"Oh, I get it now."

1856
00:57:56,392 --> 00:57:57,900
[Lesson learned from experiencing life as both prince and pauper]
Everything flipped 180 degrees.

1857
00:57:57,901 --> 00:57:59,409
People can be so cunning.

1858
00:58:00,089 --> 00:58:02,399
[SHINDONG returns as a prince after one day]
Oh, this is nice.

1859
00:58:02,400 --> 00:58:06,400
As someone who slept
in a tent the night before…

1860
00:58:06,996 --> 00:58:08,533
a bed and blankets,

1861
00:58:08,534 --> 00:58:13,133
[Even appreciating the ceiling and walls]
and the fact that everything's closed off around me is so great.

1862
00:58:13,153 --> 00:58:14,486
[Totally satisfied]
I slept so well.

1863
00:58:14,800 --> 00:58:17,600
[Even blue-blooded prince DAWN who's so used to it]
Oh, I'm a prince. I'm a prince again.

1864
00:58:18,449 --> 00:58:21,433
[The night passes
at the prince's accommodation]

1865
00:58:23,600 --> 00:58:27,167
[ALL or NOTHING]
[Day 3 status resets!]

1866
00:58:29,467 --> 00:58:32,067
[Heading to
WANGGEOZ’s final destination]

1867
00:58:33,033 --> 00:58:34,733
[Loved by the Pharaoh]

1868
00:58:34,740 --> 00:58:37,439
[The Gardens of the gods]

1869
00:58:37,967 --> 00:58:39,933
[Beneath the piercingly
blue water's surface,]

1870
00:58:41,267 --> 00:58:45,133
[the Red Sea,
home to countless marine creatures]

1871
00:58:51,600 --> 00:58:54,633
[And the unexpected scenery
beyond the shoreline]

1872
00:58:54,967 --> 00:58:58,200
[Home of the Bedouin tribe,
the masters of the desert]

1873
00:58:59,667 --> 00:59:02,833
[When the sky burns
with a fiery red sunset,]

1874
00:59:04,800 --> 00:59:08,133
[the desert transforms
constellations into a compass]

1875
00:59:08,867 --> 00:59:11,867
[Where the red desert
meets the blue Red Sea]

1876
00:59:12,367 --> 00:59:15,633
[A city full of
hot and cool surprises]

1877
00:59:15,867 --> 00:59:19,800
[HURGHADA]

1878
00:59:19,801 --> 00:59:23,767
I've never really looked at
vacation spots in Egypt

1879
00:59:23,768 --> 00:59:26,467
and really didn't know about it,
so I got curious

1880
00:59:26,468 --> 00:59:28,867
and looked up the area
we're heading to.

1881
00:59:29,197 --> 00:59:31,500
[Chill resort town vibes]
It was like Greece or places like that.

1882
00:59:31,501 --> 00:59:34,333
[Full of excitement]
I thought it'd be so nice, so I got very excited.

1883
00:59:34,513 --> 00:59:37,300
"Traveling is all about
chilling and resting."

1884
00:59:37,301 --> 00:59:38,733
That's what I was thinking.

1885
00:59:38,741 --> 00:59:41,707
And the third destination
was exactly that kind of place.

1886
00:59:41,893 --> 00:59:46,633
[With instant resort vibes]
Maldives, Bali, Phuket, or Hawaii…

1887
00:59:46,634 --> 00:59:48,000
It had those vibes,

1888
00:59:48,001 --> 00:59:49,533
[The most anticipated city during the trip]
so I was looking forward to it the most.

1889
00:59:49,695 --> 00:59:51,167
My expectations were sky-high.

1890
00:59:51,883 --> 00:59:54,300
[A totally different vibe from Cairo and Luxor]
It felt like we came to a different country.

1891
00:59:54,301 --> 00:59:56,267
The buildings
looked different too.

1892
00:59:56,673 --> 00:59:58,697
[YOHAN looked forward to some rest and relaxation]
A place to rest. A place you go to relax.

1893
00:59:58,698 --> 01:00:00,100
That's the vibe
I want to go for.

1894
01:00:00,667 --> 01:00:01,790
It was so great.

1895
01:00:01,791 --> 01:00:04,233
The reason is,
it was our chance to see the Red Sea.

1896
01:00:04,500 --> 01:00:05,900
"I'll get to see the Red Sea!"

1897
01:00:05,901 --> 01:00:07,508
[Excited about seeing the Red Sea]
"Oh, I'll get to swim in the ocean!"

1898
01:00:07,509 --> 01:00:09,967
I think I was
pretty hyped up about it.

1899
01:00:10,598 --> 01:00:13,500
[What DAWN is looking forward to]
Oh, I was really pumped for the resort vibes.

1900
01:00:13,501 --> 01:00:16,333
[About the accommodations?]
What kind of things will my accommodation have today?

1901
01:00:16,592 --> 01:00:19,206
Since I'll be a prince anyway.

1902
01:00:19,598 --> 01:00:22,333
[Even as paupers, a vacation spot sounds great]
I thought a vacation spot would be great for being a total pauper,

1903
01:00:22,500 --> 01:00:25,033
[The unique mindset of the Paupert]
since that's a whole different situation.

1904
01:00:25,200 --> 01:00:28,167
[Embracing different expectations,]
I was just thinking of fully resting at the resort.

1905
01:00:29,633 --> 01:00:33,600
[they head to
their 3rd destination, Hurghada]

1906
01:00:35,033 --> 01:00:38,533
[A quick pit stop at a rest area]

1907
01:00:39,533 --> 01:00:44,833
[They shop for souvenirs]

1908
01:00:48,933 --> 01:00:52,733
[and make local friends]
Thanks, my friend.

1909
01:00:53,622 --> 01:00:55,411
It's just really cute.
It's the Alphabet.

1910
01:00:55,412 --> 01:00:59,206
[Enjoying their free time
doing what they each like]

1911
01:00:59,207 --> 01:01:00,396
- Are you wearing it?
- What?

1912
01:01:00,675 --> 01:01:01,295
No.

1913
01:01:02,099 --> 01:01:04,900
You're still wearing
that lucky necklace.

1914
01:01:04,901 --> 01:01:07,900
[The lucky necklace merchant]
It's nicer than I thought.

1915
01:01:07,901 --> 01:01:09,500
[is ice cream shopping]

1916
01:01:09,501 --> 01:01:11,367
I'm eating Egyptian ice cream.

1917
01:01:12,593 --> 01:01:15,180
[After some time at the rest stop,]
It's my first time using dollars here.

1918
01:01:15,188 --> 01:01:16,299
What did you do?

1919
01:01:16,300 --> 01:01:17,700
I went to the bathroom.

1920
01:01:17,900 --> 01:01:19,593
I went to the bathroom,
but they asked for a dollar.

1921
01:01:21,933 --> 01:01:24,467
[they arrive
at the 3rd destination!]

1922
01:01:24,767 --> 01:01:27,600
[Hurghada Pier]

1923
01:01:27,776 --> 01:01:28,416
Have a seat.

1924
01:01:28,417 --> 01:01:32,033
[WANGGEOZ board the boat]
Taking off shoes on the boat is a new experience.

1925
01:01:33,083 --> 01:01:36,000
[The reason they boarded the boat]
Wow, the weather is so nice.

1926
01:01:36,001 --> 01:01:37,518
I'm hungry.
Let's eat as soon as we get there.

1927
01:01:37,692 --> 01:01:40,233
Today, for all of you,

1928
01:01:40,234 --> 01:01:42,084
since we've even
rented out the Luxor Temple,

1929
01:01:42,085 --> 01:01:43,294
for this shoot,

1930
01:01:43,295 --> 01:01:44,900
we also rented
an island in the Red Sea.

1931
01:01:44,901 --> 01:01:47,033
Wow! It's really beautiful.
I can give you that.

1932
01:01:47,034 --> 01:01:48,933
[Their final destination]
This view is something else.

1933
01:01:49,700 --> 01:01:52,267
[Continuing from
the cruise and the temple,]

1934
01:01:52,268 --> 01:01:55,867
[a private vacation retreat]

1935
01:01:55,868 --> 01:01:58,300
[Let's go to WANGGEOZ's very own island!]
Let's go! Let's finally go!

1936
01:01:58,301 --> 01:01:59,867
- We're going!
- Nice!

1937
01:02:02,627 --> 01:02:04,403
[Leaving the pier and heading into the Red Sea]
It really feels like we're doing something!

1938
01:02:04,404 --> 01:02:05,600
Wow!

1939
01:02:05,601 --> 01:02:07,604
It feels really different
now that the boat is moving.

1940
01:02:07,605 --> 01:02:08,998
Wow!

1941
01:02:09,271 --> 01:02:10,819
This is so great!

1942
01:02:10,820 --> 01:02:12,500
Oh, yeah!
This vibe is so nice!

1943
01:02:13,394 --> 01:02:15,687
[Can't take their eyes off of the emerald sea]
Oh!

1944
01:02:15,688 --> 01:02:17,093
That area over there
is seriously beautiful.

1945
01:02:17,393 --> 01:02:18,889
- Wow, this is amazing.
- It's not that deep.

1946
01:02:18,890 --> 01:02:19,989
- Oh! You can see that?
- Yeah.

1947
01:02:20,721 --> 01:02:23,967
It feels like we're F4 from
"Boys Over Flowers" heading over on this boat.

1948
01:02:24,500 --> 01:02:27,767
With the wind and a white sheet,
I can go anywhere.

1949
01:02:28,576 --> 01:02:29,723
This is really nice.

1950
01:02:30,323 --> 01:02:33,521
But the building colors
are different here.

1951
01:02:33,522 --> 01:02:34,733
- Oh!
- Oh, you're right.

1952
01:02:34,734 --> 01:02:36,594
[Colorful buildings]
I guess there's no sand here.

1953
01:02:36,595 --> 01:02:38,788
- That must be why.
- Because it's near the sea.

1954
01:02:39,767 --> 01:02:42,867
[Totally different colors from Cairo]
The colors are definitely different here.

1955
01:02:43,100 --> 01:02:45,233
I want to see
the Red in the Red Sea.

1956
01:02:45,234 --> 01:02:46,902
[The sunset makes the Red Sea glow red]
I want to see this fiery red sea.

1957
01:02:46,909 --> 01:02:49,101
- Later, when the sun sets.
- Yeah.

1958
01:02:49,701 --> 01:02:51,500
Wow, this is so nice.

1959
01:02:51,501 --> 01:02:53,599
- So nice!
- Wow!

1960
01:02:53,909 --> 01:02:55,399
I want to dive right here.

1961
01:02:55,400 --> 01:02:56,267
Oh!

1962
01:02:56,268 --> 01:02:59,332
- Can you do it from here?
- Yeah.

1963
01:02:59,706 --> 01:03:01,767
- It really feels like we're at a resort.
- Yeah.

1964
01:03:02,300 --> 01:03:06,700
But did ancient Egyptians think
of this place as a vacation spot?

1965
01:03:06,701 --> 01:03:08,387
Probably not.

1966
01:03:08,388 --> 01:03:11,800
Like, heading out to sea itself...

1967
01:03:11,801 --> 01:03:15,400
I doubt they would've
bothered building anything on an island.

1968
01:03:16,506 --> 01:03:18,901
I feel like the sea would've been
a completely unknown world to them.

1969
01:03:19,135 --> 01:03:21,100
Wow, the color of
the sea is insane.

1970
01:03:21,633 --> 01:03:23,800
[Trying to capture
the Red Sea on camera]

1971
01:03:23,801 --> 01:03:25,406
- It’s hard to capture it on camera, right?
- Yeah.

1972
01:03:25,407 --> 01:03:28,033
It’s nothing like what
we see with our own eyes, right?

1973
01:03:28,034 --> 01:03:29,333
Totally different.

1974
01:03:29,721 --> 01:03:32,700
[Happy]
There's even a nice breeze! This is so amazing.

1975
01:03:33,533 --> 01:03:35,197
Those people don't know
what romance is.

1976
01:03:35,198 --> 01:03:37,083
[Relentless speed with zero romance]
This right here is romance.

1977
01:03:37,084 --> 01:03:38,767
- They just want to hurry over.
- Yeah.

1978
01:03:39,467 --> 01:03:41,197
[Romantic JOHNNY
values vibes over efficiency]

1979
01:03:41,198 --> 01:03:42,600
What are you so lost in?

1980
01:03:42,700 --> 01:03:45,500
It's just so nice.

1981
01:03:45,501 --> 01:03:47,533
The wind is blowing.

1982
01:03:48,188 --> 01:03:51,133
The sea looks beautiful.

1983
01:03:51,134 --> 01:03:54,033
I feel so happy right now.

1984
01:03:55,100 --> 01:03:57,499
We gotta make time
for moments like this.

1985
01:03:57,500 --> 01:03:59,033
What do you call this again?

1986
01:03:59,034 --> 01:04:01,567
Keeping the romance alive.

1987
01:04:02,667 --> 01:04:05,233
It felt like
I stepped into a movie.

1988
01:04:05,234 --> 01:04:07,833
There was
this perfect spot on the boat.

1989
01:04:08,300 --> 01:04:12,218
I just sat there,
staring out without a single thought.

1990
01:04:12,225 --> 01:04:15,600
I also relaxed
while scrolling on my phone.

1991
01:04:16,033 --> 01:04:17,300
We also chatted together.

1992
01:04:17,500 --> 01:04:21,067
This kind of thing
is what I think is the joy of traveling.

1993
01:04:21,400 --> 01:04:24,433
It was such
a precious moment during this trip.

1994
01:04:24,900 --> 01:04:27,667
[JISUNG,
another little brother chasing romance]

1995
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:30,900
I definitely will post this.

1996
01:04:32,571 --> 01:04:33,784
This is insane, wow.

1997
01:04:35,867 --> 01:04:39,500
I think it's my first time
seeing this kind of sea from the top.

1998
01:04:46,433 --> 01:04:48,733
It's so beautiful.

1999
01:04:49,500 --> 01:04:51,300
Fish!

2000
01:04:51,301 --> 01:04:52,321
Jellyfish, jellyfish!

2001
01:04:52,322 --> 01:04:53,636
- Jellyfish, jellyfish! Oh, you're right!
- Yeah.

2002
01:04:54,103 --> 01:04:56,133
This is amazing.

2003
01:04:56,134 --> 01:04:57,100
Dolphins, dolphins!!

2004
01:04:57,300 --> 01:04:59,433
Oh?! Dolphins!!!

2005
01:04:59,667 --> 01:05:01,900
[Dolphins just
swam right next to us]

2006
01:05:02,267 --> 01:05:05,333
[The lucky dolphins
we met here in Egypt]

2007
01:05:06,167 --> 01:05:08,833
[※Added stock footage
since we couldn't film a lot※]

2008
01:05:09,833 --> 01:05:11,733
(Wow)

2009
01:05:12,500 --> 01:05:15,633
It was my first time
seeing wild dolphins.

2010
01:05:16,093 --> 01:05:20,267
It was my first time ever
experiencing something like that.

2011
01:05:20,268 --> 01:05:23,667
And the view was
just breathtaking.

2012
01:05:29,800 --> 01:05:30,900
JISUNG, you like it?

2013
01:05:30,901 --> 01:05:33,433
I love it.

2014
01:05:33,715 --> 01:05:36,100
The sea is so beautiful.

2015
01:05:36,533 --> 01:05:39,267
[By the way]
Is all of this called the Red Sea?

2016
01:05:39,268 --> 01:05:40,100
Yes!

2017
01:05:40,533 --> 01:05:41,900
How was the Red Sea parted?

2018
01:05:41,901 --> 01:05:43,200
Which way did it split?

2019
01:05:43,603 --> 01:05:44,500
It split going both ways.

2020
01:05:44,501 --> 01:05:45,500
Yeah, so it's both ways.

2021
01:05:45,501 --> 01:05:47,167
But like this, or like this?

2022
01:05:47,800 --> 01:05:50,500
[Curious which way Moses parted the Red Sea]
One land connected to the other,

2023
01:05:50,501 --> 01:05:52,200
so it must have been
from here to there.

2024
01:05:52,303 --> 01:05:54,400
- So it split like this?
- Yeah, probably.

2025
01:05:54,767 --> 01:05:57,700
But think about it.
It’s from here all the way to there.

2026
01:05:58,000 --> 01:06:00,110
Moses parted this, right?

2027
01:06:00,111 --> 01:06:02,967
Then, wouldn't it take
days to walk through it?

2028
01:06:03,200 --> 01:06:04,300
Probably just a few hours.

2029
01:06:04,301 --> 01:06:05,600
Not just a few hours, even more…!

2030
01:06:05,601 --> 01:06:07,000
I think it would take a whole day!

2031
01:06:07,001 --> 01:06:08,400
I think it's only
a few kilometers long.

2032
01:06:08,401 --> 01:06:09,700
It's only a few kilometers long?

2033
01:06:10,200 --> 01:06:12,800
[The Red Sea is vast, even at a glance]
But it's super, super far.

2034
01:06:12,801 --> 01:06:14,100
It's all the way to there!

2035
01:06:15,167 --> 01:06:17,200
(Hmm...)

2036
01:06:17,500 --> 01:06:20,333
But now that I'm here looking at it,
I think the story of splitting it

2037
01:06:20,334 --> 01:06:22,167
is nonsense.

2038
01:06:22,168 --> 01:06:23,523
[Wow, he's denying the Bible]
LEETEUK, you're gonna be in big trouble!

2039
01:06:23,524 --> 01:06:24,789
- Oh really?
- LEETEUK, that's…!

2040
01:06:25,333 --> 01:06:26,103
[Quick apology]
I'm sorry.

2041
01:06:26,104 --> 01:06:27,534
- Hey JISUNG!
- Pretend you didn't hear that.

2042
01:06:27,700 --> 01:06:31,967
[LEETEUK / Church oppa]
Everyone, I'm Christian! I mean no disrespect!

2043
01:06:31,968 --> 01:06:35,033
[Just so curious because it's so mysterious]
It's more like, how did he part this?

2044
01:06:35,216 --> 01:06:36,967
That's why it's Moses' miracle.

2045
01:06:36,968 --> 01:06:38,700
That's why
it's Moses' miracle, LEETEUK.

2046
01:06:38,701 --> 01:06:40,300
[Church oppa YOHAN
gets caught in LEETEUK’s sight]

2047
01:06:40,301 --> 01:06:40,900
Huh?

2048
01:06:41,798 --> 01:06:43,433
How do you part the Red Sea?

2049
01:06:43,800 --> 01:06:46,733
How am I supposed to know that?

2050
01:06:47,033 --> 01:06:49,400
[If you knew the method,
it wouldn't be a miracle]

2051
01:06:49,401 --> 01:06:52,733
[Damage control mode]
Now that I look at it again, I think it's possible to part.

2052
01:06:52,734 --> 01:06:55,567
[Looks doable]
I think it’s possible.

2053
01:06:55,700 --> 01:06:57,900
- Okay, acrostic poem with "Red Sea".
- Yes.

2054
01:06:57,901 --> 01:06:58,733
[Acrostic poem with "Red Sea"]
"Red"!

2055
01:06:58,734 --> 01:07:00,833
Wait,
why is this so sticky? Hold on.

2056
01:07:00,834 --> 01:07:02,333
He's stalling,
he's stalling for time.

2057
01:07:02,703 --> 01:07:03,716
"Red"!

2058
01:07:03,717 --> 01:07:04,900
"I will part the Red Sea."

2059
01:07:04,901 --> 01:07:05,900
[Excited]
Oh!

2060
01:07:05,901 --> 01:07:06,700
"Sea"!

2061
01:07:07,693 --> 01:07:09,233
"Sea it through!"

2062
01:07:09,500 --> 01:07:10,633
- Fail.
- Fail.

2063
01:07:10,634 --> 01:07:12,267
SHINDONG!
"Red"!

2064
01:07:12,268 --> 01:07:14,800
"Being here at
the Red Sea with all of you,"

2065
01:07:14,801 --> 01:07:17,500
"I think 'ALL or NOTHING' will do really well."

2066
01:07:17,501 --> 01:07:18,100
"Sea"!

2067
01:07:18,101 --> 01:07:20,167
"Sea-hee-hee-hee-hee!"

2068
01:07:20,168 --> 01:07:22,899
[Just pushing through with momentum]
You're really good at it, so good.

2069
01:07:22,906 --> 01:07:24,906
Wow, I didn't
even think about that!

2070
01:07:29,100 --> 01:07:32,067
[15 minutes since departure]

2071
01:07:32,890 --> 01:07:35,109
Is that the island
we’re heading to?

2072
01:07:35,110 --> 01:07:36,200
Is it that?

2073
01:07:36,201 --> 01:07:37,313
That way…Where exactly?

2074
01:07:37,314 --> 01:07:38,700
- Where is our island?
- Where's the island we're going to?

2075
01:07:39,192 --> 01:07:42,567
[The shape is coming into view]
I think it's that.

2076
01:07:42,633 --> 01:07:43,933
- But LEETEUK!
- Yeah?

2077
01:07:43,934 --> 01:07:45,600
There’s not a single building.

2078
01:07:45,601 --> 01:07:47,367
They said it’s not here,
but over there.

2079
01:07:47,500 --> 01:07:51,100
There’s no building there either.

2080
01:07:51,500 --> 01:07:52,900
[Staff] Why are you looking at me?

2081
01:07:52,901 --> 01:07:55,300
From what I can tell…

2082
01:07:55,301 --> 01:07:57,767
That might be the hardest place.

2083
01:07:57,900 --> 01:08:00,967
If I had to guess
the production team’s plan,

2084
01:08:00,968 --> 01:08:04,000
they seem to think
the start and the end need to be really difficult.

2085
01:08:04,719 --> 01:08:06,767
They're even taking us
to an island!

2086
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:10,300
Isn't it supposed to be
"A small beginning, a grand ending"?

2087
01:08:10,301 --> 01:08:11,567
It could really
be the most difficult one.

2088
01:08:11,880 --> 01:08:13,020
[A mission that allows the princes to leave]
Could it be that the winners

2089
01:08:13,026 --> 01:08:14,501
are the only ones
who get to leave by boat?

2090
01:08:15,634 --> 01:08:16,933
[Nervous]

2091
01:08:17,600 --> 01:08:20,433
It's really far.
We're going a really long way.

2092
01:08:20,867 --> 01:08:22,633
(Observing)

2093
01:08:23,433 --> 01:08:25,100
There’s a house, there’s a house!

2094
01:08:25,101 --> 01:08:26,200
- There is?
- Yeah, there is.

2095
01:08:26,201 --> 01:08:27,867
- What's there?
- A house!

2096
01:08:28,278 --> 01:08:29,502
- What?
- We’re sleeping there?

2097
01:08:29,503 --> 01:08:30,475
[Buildings come into view as they get closer]
It must be that!

2098
01:08:30,476 --> 01:08:32,500
- Is that it?
- Wow, that’s really huge!

2099
01:08:33,467 --> 01:08:37,500
[Giftun Island, located in the Red Sea
right in front of Hurghada]

2100
01:08:38,000 --> 01:08:41,900
[A resort for the princes]

2101
01:08:42,800 --> 01:08:45,933
[and a famous spot
with 107 parasols]

2102
01:08:47,833 --> 01:08:51,100
[Enjoy the blue Red Sea by day]

2103
01:08:51,733 --> 01:08:55,733
[And gaze at
the fiery Red Sea by night]

2104
01:08:56,833 --> 01:08:59,767
[The perfect final destination]

2105
01:09:00,133 --> 01:09:03,800
Wow, it's seriously
what you see in movies.

2106
01:09:03,801 --> 01:09:06,467
[Excited]
Wow, this is insane.

2107
01:09:06,600 --> 01:09:09,000
My heart was fluttering.

2108
01:09:09,001 --> 01:09:12,467
They said
we rented the whole island.

2109
01:09:12,700 --> 01:09:14,567
This is romance.

2110
01:09:14,733 --> 01:09:16,467
The entire island is a desert,

2111
01:09:16,468 --> 01:09:18,800
[JOHNNY] and it felt like
we used only 1/100 of it.

2112
01:09:18,801 --> 01:09:20,233
[SHINDONG] A rocky mountain
shaped by nature.

2113
01:09:20,234 --> 01:09:24,233
And a resort built
by humans right next to it.

2114
01:09:24,533 --> 01:09:26,167
Hey, I've figured it out.

2115
01:09:26,533 --> 01:09:28,500
[LEETEUK] The paupers
will sleep down there.

2116
01:09:28,501 --> 01:09:30,567
And the princes
will sleep up there.

2117
01:09:30,800 --> 01:09:32,700
Oh, they're sunbeds!

2118
01:09:32,800 --> 01:09:34,867
That's a perfect spot
for a solid 6-hour nap.

2119
01:09:34,868 --> 01:09:36,767
But it must get
so cold at night.

2120
01:09:36,768 --> 01:09:37,900
Yeah, it'll be cold at night.

2121
01:09:38,133 --> 01:09:40,000
But how can you sleep
outside today?

2122
01:09:40,001 --> 01:09:41,700
[They’re all just worried about becoming paupers]
Everyone's already worried they'll sleep outside.

2123
01:09:41,701 --> 01:09:43,366
Everyone's already
thinking about becoming paupers.

2124
01:09:43,367 --> 01:09:45,967
But being a pauper
in this setting isn't so bad!

2125
01:09:45,968 --> 01:09:47,733
The sand is your bed.

2126
01:09:47,734 --> 01:09:50,267
The wind is your blanket.

2127
01:09:50,268 --> 01:09:54,133
[Completely forgot his life as a pauper]
LEETEUK, have you forgotten how it was after just two days?

2128
01:09:54,333 --> 01:09:56,500
But today,
I really don't need to be a prince.

2129
01:09:56,501 --> 01:09:57,300
You don't?

2130
01:09:57,301 --> 01:09:58,700
I'm fine today.

2131
01:09:58,701 --> 01:09:59,900
- Really?
- Oh, really?

2132
01:09:59,901 --> 01:10:01,867
[But if you make me one, I'll be one]
I mean, I wouldn't say no.

2133
01:10:02,300 --> 01:10:03,333
I want to be a prince.

2134
01:10:03,633 --> 01:10:05,400
Is someone letting you?

2135
01:10:08,100 --> 01:10:08,800
Let's go!

2136
01:10:08,801 --> 01:10:10,867
[30 minutes after leaving Hurghada]
Let’s go, let’s go!

2137
01:10:11,800 --> 01:10:14,567
[Arrived at the island where the last prince will be decided!]
Wow, this is cool.

2138
01:10:14,568 --> 01:10:17,267
[DAWN] The big boat couldn't go closer,
so we took a smaller boat

2139
01:10:17,268 --> 01:10:21,833
to head to the island's dock,
and it felt like a movie.

2140
01:10:23,305 --> 01:10:24,411
Wow, so cool.

2141
01:10:24,805 --> 01:10:25,819
This is awesome.

2142
01:10:25,820 --> 01:10:26,700
Wow, this is insane.

2143
01:10:26,701 --> 01:10:28,033
I feel like we just
stepped onto a movie set.

2144
01:10:28,400 --> 01:10:30,300
[WANGGEOZ finally arrives on land]
Wow!

2145
01:10:30,301 --> 01:10:32,699
- Wow, this is crazy.
- This place is next level!

2146
01:10:32,700 --> 01:10:33,700
This is the place!

2147
01:10:34,000 --> 01:10:36,109
- This is the spot!
- The view is crazy!

2148
01:10:36,367 --> 01:10:38,200
Seeing that there are
this many sunbeds,

2149
01:10:38,201 --> 01:10:40,433
it means that
this many people come here.

2150
01:10:40,533 --> 01:10:42,414
[Giftun Island, a tourist hotspot in the Red Sea]
Honestly, I think I could totally sleep here too.

2151
01:10:42,415 --> 01:10:43,515
But I feel like
you'd end up eating a ton of sand.

2152
01:10:43,516 --> 01:10:44,529
It'd be so cold.

2153
01:10:44,530 --> 01:10:46,100
Yes, it'd be so cold.

2154
01:10:47,400 --> 01:10:48,797
Wow!

2155
01:10:48,798 --> 01:10:50,112
Oh, it’s way bigger!

2156
01:10:50,113 --> 01:10:51,900
[Up close, the scale is next level]
Oh, this place is huge!

2157
01:10:51,901 --> 01:10:53,500
Look!
There are individual rooms over there.

2158
01:10:54,100 --> 01:10:57,300
[When you pass the parasols and head inside,]
Wow, the building is massive!

2159
01:10:57,967 --> 01:10:59,296
[you can see the princes' rooms]

2160
01:10:59,297 --> 01:11:01,533
I'd be so happy
waking up here in the morning.

2161
01:11:01,800 --> 01:11:03,600
This is so nice.

2162
01:11:05,478 --> 01:11:08,100
Then, we're the only ones
on this island?

2163
01:11:08,101 --> 01:11:09,100
It feels like it's just us.

2164
01:11:09,200 --> 01:11:11,582
[The princes’ holiday on a private island]
Wow, that view over there is stunning too.

2165
01:11:11,583 --> 01:11:13,210
Wow!

2166
01:11:13,300 --> 01:11:14,800
Wow, this place is so beautiful.

2167
01:11:15,183 --> 01:11:16,298
This is a view hotspot!

2168
01:11:16,299 --> 01:11:17,200
This is insane.

2169
01:11:18,192 --> 01:11:19,300
It feels unreal.

2170
01:11:21,733 --> 01:11:24,500
- I need to check that area out.
- Wow, this is so cool.

2171
01:11:24,720 --> 01:11:26,388
- Wow!
- Wow!

2172
01:11:27,407 --> 01:11:28,233
This is amazing!

2173
01:11:28,433 --> 01:11:31,267
[Moving on to the princes’ rooms]
Oh, the rooms are here.

2174
01:11:31,589 --> 01:11:32,975
Oh, wow!

2175
01:11:32,976 --> 01:11:33,995
That’s right.

2176
01:11:34,499 --> 01:11:36,067
Oh!

2177
01:11:36,068 --> 01:11:38,511
Whoa!

2178
01:11:38,685 --> 01:11:41,400
Whoa, there’s a terrace!

2179
01:11:41,967 --> 01:11:45,000
[When you enter a prince's room,]

2180
01:11:45,633 --> 01:11:48,033
[there's crisp, fresh bedding]

2181
01:11:48,767 --> 01:11:51,633
[and an ocean view
you can enjoy lying down]

2182
01:11:54,567 --> 01:11:58,300
[A place with a view like this]

2183
01:12:02,367 --> 01:12:04,100
I need to be a prince.

2184
01:12:04,101 --> 01:12:06,500
(Legendary)
This is one room, like this? Wow, amazing!

2185
01:12:06,501 --> 01:12:07,600
Wow!

2186
01:12:07,601 --> 01:12:11,000
[LEETEUK] In the morning,
you step out here with a coffee in hand…!

2187
01:12:11,411 --> 01:12:14,333
- Wow, this is crazy.
- This place is so beautiful.

2188
01:12:14,600 --> 01:12:16,400
[Happy]
Wow!

2189
01:12:16,600 --> 01:12:17,893
Is that a pool over there?

2190
01:12:17,894 --> 01:12:18,900
- Wow!
- Oh, you're right.

2191
01:12:18,901 --> 01:12:22,733
[A pool facing the Red Sea]

2192
01:12:25,000 --> 01:12:27,300
They said
there are welcome drinks here.

2193
01:12:27,301 --> 01:12:28,200
Oh, please!

2194
01:12:28,817 --> 01:12:30,318
- Wow!
- Wow!

2195
01:12:30,593 --> 01:12:31,513
Thank you!

2196
01:12:31,888 --> 01:12:32,695
Welcome drinks?

2197
01:12:32,696 --> 01:12:36,433
[Welcome to Giftun Island]
Pineapple.

2198
01:12:37,130 --> 01:12:38,233
Shall we clink glasses?

2199
01:12:38,617 --> 01:12:39,384
Sounds good.

2200
01:12:40,472 --> 01:12:42,032
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

2201
01:12:42,033 --> 01:12:45,400
- "ALL or NOTHING"!
- "ALL or NOTHING"!

2202
01:12:47,009 --> 01:12:48,400
- Wow!
- This is so delicious!

2203
01:12:49,000 --> 01:12:50,310
Oh, I'm just so happy.

2204
01:12:50,311 --> 01:12:52,800
[What kind of fierce battle
will unfold in this calm and relaxed vibe?]

2205
01:12:52,801 --> 01:12:54,191
Hey, I have to be a prince today.

2206
01:12:57,503 --> 01:12:58,896
[What are you doing...?]
Hey, hurry up!

2207
01:12:58,897 --> 01:12:59,767
No, like why…?

2208
01:12:59,768 --> 01:13:02,095
[What arrived instead of a fierce battle is]
Why are you so happy? Why so happy?

2209
01:13:02,096 --> 01:13:04,767
[Happiness?!]
No, like, why are you so happy?

2210
01:13:05,800 --> 01:13:08,900
[All the foods you wanted in one place!]
I can’t resist ramyun! I just can’t!

2211
01:13:08,901 --> 01:13:10,402
[This is paradise!]
Wow, this is seriously delicious.

2212
01:13:10,403 --> 01:13:11,900
Egypt really knows
how to make a good burger.

2213
01:13:12,726 --> 01:13:14,102
[Relaxed laughter
just comes naturally now]

2214
01:13:14,103 --> 01:13:15,415
We're reporting live on location!

2215
01:13:15,608 --> 01:13:17,290
[When was the last time we were this relaxed…?]
I'm really taking in all of Egypt.

2216
01:13:17,298 --> 01:13:18,685
Oh, then…

2217
01:13:18,900 --> 01:13:22,267
[A paradise on earth instead of a fierce battle]
This is fun, this is fun.

2218
01:13:26,596 --> 01:13:27,309
Wow!

2219
01:13:30,484 --> 01:13:31,604
I should’ve come out alone.

2220
01:13:32,385 --> 01:13:35,133
[The final hurdle to becoming a prince]
What? How do you play this game?

2221
01:13:35,267 --> 01:13:37,433
[A conversation with the ancients]

2222
01:13:37,434 --> 01:13:39,467
[Search through the whole island]
Those who find and understand the ancient language

2223
01:13:39,468 --> 01:13:41,600
[and find the hidden clues]
will become princes.

2224
01:13:41,601 --> 01:13:43,700
I really can’t trust LEETEUK…

2225
01:13:43,701 --> 01:13:45,067
[If you want to become a prince,]
Let’s just show one each.

2226
01:13:45,068 --> 01:13:46,688
[do whatever it takes]
Want to share? I’ll solve the question for you!

2227
01:13:46,689 --> 01:13:49,200
If we keep going like this,
we could both become princes.

2228
01:13:49,407 --> 01:13:50,789
[A relentless onslaught]
Please, please!

2229
01:13:50,796 --> 01:13:52,388
[of an intense showdown]
JISUNG!

2230
01:13:52,389 --> 01:13:53,200
Throw it away.

2231
01:13:54,200 --> 01:13:56,200
Seriously, no way!
But…this is really not it.

2232
01:13:56,293 --> 01:13:58,713
[Who will be the final prince?]
Wow, then I'm gonna be traumatized for the rest of my life.

2233
01:13:58,721 --> 01:13:59,693
I can’t stand stuff like this.
